The '''Hennessey Venom F5''' is a [[sports car]] developed and manufactured by the American vehicle-manufacturing company [[Hennessey Special Vehicles]] which was established in 2017.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://hennesseyperformance.com/about/john-hennessey/ |title=Hennessey Special Vehicles |publisher=Hennessey Performance |location=US |date=2018-10-02 |access-date=2018-10-02}}</ref> Contracted with [[Delta Motorsport]] of Silverstone, England for the development of the vehicle, this is Hennessey's first all new proprietary vehicle as an accredited titled manufacturer.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.autosflux.com/2019-hennessey-venom-f5/ |title=2019 Hennessey Venom F5 Review - Pictures, Specification and Features |website=Autos Flux |date=2019-09-22 |access-date=2020-02-29}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|url=http://hennesseyperformance.com/hennessey-considers-venom-f5-roadster-as-coupe-production-begins/|title=Hennessey Considers Venom F5 Roadster As Coupe Production Begins {{!}} Hennessey Performance |language=en-US|access-date=2019-10-30}}</ref>  The F5 name is a reference to the highest rating on the [[Fujita scale]]: F5, designated to [[tornado]]es that have attained wind speeds as high as {{cvt|261–318|mph|km/h|0}}.<ref name=":0">{{cite news |last=Cenizo |first=Sebastian |date=2021-10-08 |title=Hennessey Designer Shows Off The Venom F5's Intricate Details |url=https://carbuzz.com/news/hennessey-designer-shows-off-the-venom-f5s-intricate-details |access-date=2021-10-27 |work=CarBuzz |location=US}}</ref>

Hennessey aims to reach top speeds in excess of {{cvt|311|mph|km/h|round=5}} to attain the title of [[Production car speed record|world's fastest production car]].<ref>{{cite news |url= https://news.dupontregistry.com/news/hennessey-venom-f5-price-specs-review/ |title=Hennessey F5 Venom: Forget 300 mph, aiming for 311 mph; challengers welcome |first=Joel |last=Feder |work=Motor Authority |location=US |date=2018-09-26 |access-date=2021-10-27}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|url=https://autonxt.net/hennessey-venom-f5-all-american-hypercar/|title = Hennessey Venom F5 — All-American Hypercar|date = 15 December 2020}}</ref><ref>{{cite web | url=https://www.motorauthority.com/news/1118952_hennessey-f5-venom-forget-300-mph-aiming-for-311-mph-challengers-welcome | title=Hennessey F5 Venom: Forget 300 MPH, aiming for 311 MPH; challengers welcome | date=September 26, 2018 }}</ref>

