The [[engine]] used in the Venom F5 is the ''Fury'' designed and manufactured by Hennessey. The ''Fury'' is a [[twin-turbo]] 6.6 L [[V8 engine|V8]], that produces up to {{convert|1817|hp|PS kW|0|abbr=on}} and {{convert|1193|lbft|Nm|0|abbr=on}}.<ref name="specs"/> In April 2025, Hennessey released the Evolution package, costing an extra $285,000, which increases the power output to {{convert|2031|hp|PS kW|0|abbr=on}} by using E85 fuel. Cars fitted with this upgrade are claimed to be capable of accelerating from {{Convert|0-200|mph|kph|0|abbr=on}} in 10.3 seconds.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Hennessey Finalizes Testing of 2031 HP 'Venom F5 Evolution' Hypercar |url=https://www.hennesseyspecialvehicles.com/news/hennessey-finalizes-testing-of-2031-hp-venom-f5-evolution-hypercar/ |website=Hennessey Special Vehicles}}</ref>

[[Costruzione Italiana Macchine Attrezzi]] provides the available 7-speed single-clutch [[automated manual transmission]] with paddle-shifters and the [[limited-slip differential]] sending power to the rear wheels, making the car [[rear-wheel drive]].<ref>{{Cite news |last=Bovingdon |first=Jethro |date=2020-12-15 |title=Snake Juice: Hennessey Venom F5 Is a 1,800-HP, 311-MPH Hypercar |url=https://www.motortrend.com/news/hennessey-venom-f5-first-look-review |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240329235738/https://www.motortrend.com/news/hennessey-venom-f5-first-look-review/ |archive-date=2024-03-29  |work=[[MotorTrend]] |language=en-US |access-date=2025-04-25  |url-status=live }}</ref><ref name="AutoBlog-20187-11-01">{{cite news |last=Gustafson |first=Sven |date=November 1, 2017 |title=301 mph, 1,600 hp: Hennessey Venom F5 details emerge |url=https://www.autoblog.com/2017/11/01/301-mph-1-600-hp-hennessey-venom-f5-details-emerge/ |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20171104161929/https://www.autoblog.com/2017/11/01/301-mph-1-600-hp-hennessey-venom-f5-details-emerge/ |archive-date=2017-11-04 |website=[[Autoblog (website)|Autoblog]] |location=US}}</ref>

The chassis and body is made almost entirely of [[carbon fiber]]. Active aerodynamics are removed in the production car, replaced with a smaller fixed spoiler. The three exhausts in the concept model was changed to four exhausts. The car's weight reportedly stands at {{convert|2950|lbs|kg|0|abbr=on}} with fluids, setting the power-to-weight ratio at 1,358&nbsp;hp per ton.<ref>{{cite news |url=https://www.motor1.com/news/374004/hennessey-venom-f5-horsepower-rating/ |title=Hennessey Venom F5 Engine Rated At 1,817 Horsepower |work=Motor1 |publisher=[[Motorsport Network]] |date=October 2, 2019 |access-date=October 2, 2019}}</ref> Because of the use of active aerodynamics and a sleek, new design in the concept model, the car has an estimated {{Cd|long=yes|link=car|0.33}}.<ref name=TopGear-2017-11-01>{{Cite magazine |url=https://www.topgear.com/car-news/first-look/new-hennessey-venom-f5-aims-300mph |title=New Hennessey Venom F5 aims for 300mph |first=Rowan |last=Horncastle |magazine=[[Top Gear (magazine)|Top Gear]] |publisher=[[BBC]] |location=UK |date=November 1, 2017 |access-date=November 1, 2017 |archive-date=2017-11-07  |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20171107003025/https://www.topgear.com/car-news/first-look/new-hennessey-venom-f5-aims-300mph |url-status=dead }}</ref> The production variant is claimed to have an increased drag coefficient of {{Cd|0.39}}.<ref>{{cite news |url=https://www.autoexpress.co.uk/news/101407/hennessey-venom-f5-new-high-speed-testing-video |title=Hennessey Venom F5 in new high-speed testing video |first=Luke |last=Wilkinson |work=Auto Express |location=UK |date=January 11, 2022 |access-date=August 13, 2022}}</ref>

According to Hennessey, great emphasis was placed on interior space, quality and comfort, so that despite offering high performance, the vehicle would still offer a spacious and comfortable interior experience that can accommodate tall and large drivers and passengers. It was mentioned that an undisclosed NFL player, who has only been described as being 6'7" tall, has placed an order for one of the first models once full production has commenced.<ref>{{cite magazine |url=https://topgear.com.my/new-hennessey-venom-f5-aims-for-483kph |title=New Hennessey Venom F5 aims for 483kph |magazine=[[Top Gear (magazine)|Top Gear Malaysia]] |location=Malaysia |access-date=November 1, 2017 |archive-date=2021-10-11  |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211011212606/https://topgear.com.my/new-hennessey-venom-f5-aims-for-483kph |url-status=dead }}</ref>

Each Venom F5 comes with the "Treasure Chest", a giant aluminum box containing the key fob, a [[Trickle charging|magnetic trickle charger]], and a tow hook. The key fob's serial number plate is made from a metal component that was disposed from a [[Space Shuttle]] launch. Company founder John Hennessey was given the component by an astronaut and broke it into pieces to give Venom F5 owners "a piece of space".<ref>{{cite AV media |url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=z4YQeGeNdPk |title=The Hennessey Venom F5 Is an Ultra-Rare $2 Million+ Hypercar |author-link=Doug DeMuro |last=DeMuro |first=Doug |publisher=[[YouTube]] |date=June 28, 2022 |access-date=June 29, 2022}}</ref>

