== Production ==
The first production was limited to 24 units, 12 of which were already sold by December 2020. The price of the car in the United States was initially {{USD|1.6 million}}, but later increased to {{USD|2.1 million}} for the remaining 12 units.<ref name="CD2020">{{Cite web|url=https://www.caranddriver.com/news/a34961869/hennessey-venom-f5-revealed/|title=1817-HP Hennessey Venom F5 Revealed, Claims 311-MPH Top Speed|work=[[Car and Driver]]|last=Duff|first=Mike|date=2020-12-15}}</ref> Eight cars are planned to be built and delivered in 2021. In August 2021 the company officially announced that it had customer orders for and had sold all planned 24 units of the F5.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://carbuzz.com/news/sorry-the-hennessey-venom-f5-is-sold-out|title = Sorry, the Hennessey Venom F5 is Sold Out |date=2021-08-19}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|url=http://hennesseyperformance.com/official-the-2-1m-hennessey-venom-f5-has-sold-out/|title = Official: The $2.1m Hennessey Venom F5 has sold out &#124; Hennessey Performance}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.hennesseyspecialvehicles.com/hennessey-announces-venom-f5-hypercar-is-sold-out/ |title=Hennessey Announces Venom F5 Hypercar is Sold Out |date=2021-08-19}}</ref>

The Hennessey Venom F5 Revolution was limited to 36 units, consisting of 24 Coupes and 12 Roadsters; Hennessey has stated that the Roadster allocations are sold out already.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Guerra |first=Baltazar |date=2023-08-08 |title=Hennessey Reveals Stunning Venom F5 'Revolution Roadster' Hypercar in Bare Carbon |url=https://www.hennesseymedia.com/press-releases/hennessey-reveals-stunning-venom-f5-revolution-roadster-hypercar-in-bare-carbon/ |access-date=2025-12-03 |website=Hennessey Media |language=en-US}}</ref> The Revolution variant undergoes extensive re-engineering for improved track capability, including revised aerodynamics, retuned suspension, lightweight wheels, a roof-mounted air intake, and onboard digital telemetry.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Mcafee |first=Rex |date=2023-01-10 |title=Hennessey Unveils Venom F5 “Revolution” |url=https://www.supercars.net/blog/hennessey-unveils-venom-f5-revolution/ |access-date=2025-12-03 |website=Supercars.net |language=en-US}}</ref> With an approximate price of $2.7 million, the model focuses on enhanced handling and weight reduction compared to the standard Venom F5.

Development of the Venom F5 Revolution was led by John “Heinrocket” Heinricy, Hennessey's Chief Engineer and former General Motors performance specialist known for the Cadillac CTS-V and Chevrolet Corvette Z06. Heinricy stated that designing the Revolution surpassed his prior engineering projects, emphasizing its ultra-lightweight construction and extreme power.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Mauricio |date=2023-01-09 |title=Hennessey Unveils Apex Track-Focused Venom F5 'Revolution' Hypercar |url=https://www.hennesseymedia.com/press-releases/hennessey-unveils-apex-track-focused-venom-f5-revolution-hypercar/ |access-date=2025-12-03 |website=Hennessey Media |language=en-US}}</ref> Hennessey's Maverick division built a one-of-one edition called the Venom F5 Revolution LF.<ref>{{Cite web |date=2025-08-15 |title=Hennessey Unveils 1-of-1 Manual Venom F5 Hypercar with 2,031 Horsepower |url=https://www.hennesseyspecialvehicles.com/news/hennessey-unveils-1-of-1-manual-venom-f5-hypercar-with-2031-horsepower/ |access-date=2025-12-03 |language=en-US}}</ref>

In April 2025 Hennessey revealed the {{cvt|2,031|hp|kW|0}} Venom F5 Evolution model.<ref>{{Cite web |date=2025-04-16 |title=Hennessey Finalizes Testing of 2031 HP ‘Venom F5 Evolution’ Hypercar |url=https://www.hennesseyspecialvehicles.com/news/hennessey-finalizes-testing-of-2031-hp-venom-f5-evolution-hypercar/ |access-date=2026-10-15 |language=en-US}}</ref>

