== World record ==
On July 30, 2024, the Venom F5 broke the standing {{convert|1/2|mile|m|0|abbr=out}} record for production cars with a time of 14.44 seconds at {{cvt|353|km/h|mph|order=flip}}. This record was set in Florida, United States driven by John Hennessey.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://fastestlaps.com/models/hennessey-venom-f5 |title=Hennessey Venom F5 specs, 0-60, quarter mile |website=Fastest Laps |access-date=2024-09-06}}</ref>

